<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16156" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσήμ-αντος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without leader</i> or
				<i>shepherd,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήλοισιν ἀσημάντοισιν ἐπελθών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.485
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Tryph.
				616
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					3.361
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>unsealed, unmarked,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.38
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				954a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				4
			</span></i>; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφύλακτος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>giving no sign</i>: hence, <i>unseen, unknown,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				3.95
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.232
			</span></i>; <i>unintelligible,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπεα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				10.31
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσήμαντοι τούτου ὃ . . σῶμα ὀνομάζομεν</span>
			<i>not entombed</i> in this, which we call body, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				250c
			</span></i>, with play on signf. <i><span class="en">
				11.1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				161
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>uncoined,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσὸς καὶ ἄργυρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>Hisp.</u>
					23
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				<u>Pun.</u>
				66
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b>
			
				Act.
			, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σημαντικός,</span>
			<i>without significance,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diog.Bab.Stoic.
					3.213
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωνή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.1026a
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paul.Aeg.
					3.15
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
